      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2015 Cleveland Clinic.",
        "AbstractText": "Outcomes and long-term survival rates after liver transplantation have significantly improved over the last 5 decades, but the improved longevity is accompanied by long-term complications such as metabolic syndrome, obesity, cardiovascular disease, cancer, and bone disease. After the first year, the primary care physician assumes a greater role and provides most of the patient's care. This review provides a source for primary care physicians in managing the long-term medical complications seen in these patients."
      },
